  @key-example
  Scenario: Agent receives and executes an explore command
    Given the Architect Agent is registered with the fleet
    When a CommandPayload arrives with command "explore"
      | field                  | value                    |
      | args.codebase_path     | /path/to/codebase        |
      | args.architecture_path | /path/to/ARCHITECTURE.md |
      | args.query             | drift check              |
      | correlation_id         | cmd-explore-789          |
    Then the agent should invoke the exploration session handler
    And a ResultPayload should be published with correlation_id "cmd-explore-789"

  # Why: Agent-to-agent feasibility is the canonical cross-agent workflow —
  # a Product Owner asks the Architect "can we build this?"
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Agent receives a feasibility check from another agent
    Given the Architect Agent is registered with the fleet
    When a CommandPayload arrives with command "feasibility"
      | field                | value                                          |
      | args.idea_summary    | Add real-time fraud scoring to pipeline         |
      | args.constraints     | ["Must integrate with NATS", "<200ms latency"] |
